    "reactants": {
      "caption": "the lactol (both OH groups as THP ethers) + the ylide of (4-carboxybutyl)triphenylphosphonium (as its carboxylate) + sodium dimsyl in DMSO",
      "hintTiers": [
        "The ylide reacts with aldehydes, but a lactol is a cyclic hemiacetal. The open hydroxy-aldehyde forms when the lactol O–H is deprotonated and the ring opens.",
        "The dimsyl anion (CH₃S(O)CH₂⁻), a strong base, takes the proton of the lactol OH.",
        "Dimsyl carbon lone pair → new bond to the lactol O–H hydrogen; that O–H bond → lone pair on oxygen."
      ],
      "mappedSmiles": "[O:1]([CH:2]1[O:3][C@H:4]2[CH2:5][C@@H:6]([O:7][CH:60]3[O:61][CH2:62][CH2:63][CH2:64][CH2:65]3)[C@H:8](/[CH:9]=[CH:10]/[C@@H:11]([O:12][CH:70]3[O:71][CH2:72][CH2:73][CH2:74][CH2:75]3)[CH2:13][CH2:14][CH2:15][CH2:16][CH3:17])[C@H:18]2[CH2:20]1)[H:19].[CH-:30]([P+:31]([C:40]1=[CH:41][CH:42]=[CH:43][CH:44]=[CH:45]1)([C:46]1=[CH:47][CH:48]=[CH:49][CH:50]=[CH:51]1)[C:52]1=[CH:53][CH:54]=[CH:55][CH:56]=[CH:57]1)[CH2:32][CH2:33][CH2:34][C:35](=[O:36])[O-:37].[Na+:38].[CH2-:80][S:81](=[O:82])[CH3:83].[Na+:84]",
