  ],
  "reactionVersion": 2,
  "mechanismSummary": "DIBAL reduced the lactone to the lactol (not drawn). The Wittig reagent comes from (4-carboxybutyl)triphenylphosphonium bromide and two equivalents of sodium dimsyl in DMSO: one removes the CO₂H proton and one the P–CH₂ proton. The lactol is a masked aldehyde: deprotonation and ring opening reveal the CHO, and the ylide adds to it through an oxaphosphetane, which falls apart to Ph₃P=O and the alkene. An unstabilised ylide under salt-free conditions gives the (Z)-alkene, the cis double bond of PGF₂α (explained, not yet checked by the app). Acid work-up protonates the alkoxide and the carboxylate, and aqueous acetic acid removes both THP groups to give prostaglandin F₂α. THP (tetrahydropyranyl) is drawn as a label: it takes no part.",
